1
00:00:01,148 --> 00:00:02,218
Oh, and Gwon Sik.

2
00:00:03,318 --> 00:00:05,188
I have something to ask you.

3
00:00:09,318 --> 00:00:10,388
It's about that child.

4
00:00:14,228 --> 00:00:17,258
Do you happen to know what happened to him?

5
00:00:18,698 --> 00:00:19,928
What child?

6
00:00:20,568 --> 00:00:22,338
The child from 25 years ago.

7
00:00:22,968 --> 00:00:24,498
The one who survived the accident.

8
00:00:26,638 --> 00:00:28,808
Why do you ask about that child?

9
00:00:29,508 --> 00:00:32,348
I suddenly got curious.

10
00:00:34,308 --> 00:00:36,078
How would I know that?

11
00:00:36,718 --> 00:00:39,188
I was sent straight to prison back then,

12
00:00:40,388 --> 00:00:43,488
and I was not out in the world for five years.

13
00:00:50,198 --> 00:00:52,468
Last time, I asked you if Team Leader Ko...

14
00:00:52,968 --> 00:00:55,638
was the son of someone the Chairman knew.

15
00:00:56,768 --> 00:00:58,538
But it turns out Team Leader Ko's father...

16
00:00:59,168 --> 00:01:03,038
was the head of design at Gangsu Construction.

17
00:01:04,708 --> 00:01:05,978
You really did not know?

18
00:01:06,908 --> 00:01:10,648
His photo was in the video at the Chairman's living funeral.

19
00:01:16,318 --> 00:01:17,318
Sung Jun.

20
00:01:19,888 --> 00:01:21,958
Look at this. There they go again.

21
00:01:22,428 --> 00:01:25,998
How is it that the moment I walk in, the conversation just stops?

22
00:01:26,398 --> 00:01:27,898
What brings you to the secretary's office?

23
00:01:28,428 --> 00:01:29,898
Well, I have something to discuss

24
00:01:29,968 --> 00:01:31,638
with Chief Secretary Seo for a moment.

25
00:01:31,968 --> 00:01:34,568
Secretary Jo, I am sorry, but can you go to the first-floor cafe...

26
00:01:34,908 --> 00:01:37,078
and get that drink I ordered last time?

27
00:01:37,408 --> 00:01:40,648
The Iced Salted Caramel Hazelnut Mascarpone...

28
00:01:40,708 --> 00:01:41,708
In that case,

29
00:01:42,878 --> 00:01:44,048
I will step out for a moment.

30
00:01:45,518 --> 00:01:47,148
Okay. Thank you.

31
00:01:48,148 --> 00:01:51,588
Wow. I guess it is because he is so smart.

32
00:01:51,918 --> 00:01:53,428
He is quick on the uptake too.

33
00:01:54,258 --> 00:01:56,758
Go ahead. What is it you have to say to me?

34
00:01:57,498 --> 00:02:00,328
On the day of my father's living funeral,

35
00:02:01,228 --> 00:02:02,667
Gyeol was on a call,

36
00:02:02,668 --> 00:02:04,898
and I saw his expression suddenly change.

37
00:02:05,768 --> 00:02:06,968
What was Gyeol's call about?

38
00:02:09,278 --> 00:02:11,878
What's with you? Why are you not answering my question?

39
00:02:13,308 --> 00:02:14,377
It was a call...

40
00:02:14,378 --> 00:02:16,178
from the Jeongbin Police Station Traffic Investigation Unit.

41
00:02:17,518 --> 00:02:18,848
Jeongbin Police Station?

42
00:02:19,488 --> 00:02:21,648
Why would they call Gyeol?

43
00:02:22,188 --> 00:02:25,158
Gyeol was looking for his father's case file.

44
00:02:26,828 --> 00:02:30,328
Why's he looking into something from 25 years ago now?

45
00:02:30,958 --> 00:02:31,998
I wonder.

46
00:02:33,128 --> 00:02:34,798
He probably wants to know the truth.

47
00:02:36,838 --> 00:02:38,368
Goodness.

48
00:02:38,908 --> 00:02:40,238
So, what are you going to do?

49
00:02:40,968 --> 00:02:42,038
What do you mean by that?

50
00:02:42,378 --> 00:02:44,738
Well, if he digs into the case file,

51
00:02:44,838 --> 00:02:46,477
he is going to find out that you are the one...

52
00:02:46,478 --> 00:02:47,678
who killed his father.

53
00:02:48,718 --> 00:02:51,878
- Gyeol trusted and relied on you? - Sir!

54
00:02:53,188 --> 00:02:54,318
Why? What?

55
00:02:55,048 --> 00:02:57,658
What? Am I wrong?

56
00:02:58,388 --> 00:03:00,828
It is true, is it not? You are the culprit.

57
00:03:05,898 --> 00:03:09,168
But it is not like it will be easy for him to find out.

58
00:03:09,338 --> 00:03:12,638
So much time has passed. I doubt any information is left.

59
00:03:14,168 --> 00:03:15,608
Do not worry. It is fine.

60
00:03:17,308 --> 00:03:20,678
What do you think will happen if Gyeol finds out?

61
00:03:21,978 --> 00:03:24,048
- What? - The truth will out.

62
00:03:25,078 --> 00:03:26,848
I believe that is what you told me last time.

63
00:03:28,218 --> 00:03:30,758
Look, I know you must think I'm a nobody.

64
00:03:30,988 --> 00:03:34,628
I heard she was adopted overseas. To France or someplace, right?

65
00:03:38,028 --> 00:03:41,268
Gwon Sik, secrets don't stay secret forever.

66
00:03:41,728 --> 00:03:45,168
However hard you try to hide it, the truth comes out eventually.

67
00:03:46,608 --> 00:03:47,638
You...

68
00:03:48,108 --> 00:03:50,508
You know the saying about an awl in a pocket?

69
00:03:51,278 --> 00:03:52,648
Then you can see for yourself when that happens.

70
00:03:53,278 --> 00:03:55,108
When the awl finally pokes through the pocket.

71
00:03:56,978 --> 00:03:58,078
What does that mean?

72
00:03:58,848 --> 00:04:00,288
Why are you saying that to me?

73
00:04:07,388 --> 00:04:08,388
Yes, Chairman.

74
00:04:09,328 --> 00:04:10,498
I will see you later.

75
00:04:11,228 --> 00:04:12,228
Yes.

76
00:04:14,368 --> 00:04:16,438
What? Is my father calling for you?

77
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:19,668
If you have nothing more to say, please leave.

78
00:04:19,738 --> 00:04:22,738
Hey. This is my company. Who are you to tell me to leave?

79
00:04:26,748 --> 00:04:28,448
I am warning you again.

80
00:04:29,778 --> 00:04:31,118
Don't do anything reckless.

81
00:04:31,878 --> 00:04:32,888
Understand?

82
00:04:42,198 --> 00:04:44,658
What? "An awl in a pocket?"

83
00:04:45,328 --> 00:04:47,528
You need to get stabbed by that awl in your own pocket...

84
00:04:47,598 --> 00:04:48,628
to knock some sense into you.

85
00:04:52,568 --> 00:04:53,568
Yes, Father.

86
00:04:54,368 --> 00:04:56,308
This is the file with the project budget summary...

87
00:04:56,378 --> 00:04:57,508
for each candidate site.

88
00:04:58,038 --> 00:05:01,278
Please review it to see if the budget execution is feasible.

89
00:05:01,678 --> 00:05:03,518
All right, just leave it there. I'll look over it later.

90
00:05:03,778 --> 00:05:04,778
Yes, sir.

91
00:05:05,278 --> 00:05:08,118
But what's wrong? Did something bad happen?

92
00:05:08,518 --> 00:05:09,518
Hey.

93
00:05:10,288 --> 00:05:12,188
Tell Team Leader Ko to come to my office.

94
00:05:12,728 --> 00:05:13,728
Right now.

95
00:05:13,788 --> 00:05:15,998
Team Leader Ko took a half-day off. He's not here.

96
00:05:16,058 --> 00:05:17,397
What? A half-day?

97
00:05:17,398 --> 00:05:18,728
With the third competition coming up,

98
00:05:18,798 --> 00:05:20,798
what on earth is he doing taking a half-day off?

99
00:05:21,068 --> 00:05:23,198
Actually, Gyeol has been...

100
00:05:23,498 --> 00:05:26,408
looking for the case file on his biological father's death.

101
00:05:27,138 --> 00:05:29,478
What? Does he think this company is a joke?

102
00:05:30,178 --> 00:05:31,537
The competition is right around the corner,

103
00:05:31,538 --> 00:05:33,278
and he's taking time off for personal matters?

104
00:05:33,648 --> 00:05:35,078
Why are you so upset?

105
00:05:35,348 --> 00:05:37,948
But Gyeol is working hard to prepare for the competition.

106
00:05:38,018 --> 00:05:39,187
Then why is someone so dedicated...

107
00:05:39,188 --> 00:05:41,048
so obsessed with something from 25 years ago?

108
00:05:41,148 --> 00:05:43,218
Tell him to get back to the office now. Immediately!

109
00:05:51,428 --> 00:05:53,168
It says the case file is still on record.

110
00:05:53,498 --> 00:05:55,098
Please fill out the application to view and copy the records.

111
00:05:55,698 --> 00:05:56,968
Okay, I will.

112
00:05:57,068 --> 00:05:59,207
The prosecutor in charge will review your application

113
00:05:59,208 --> 00:06:01,138
to decide if access will be granted,

114
00:06:01,208 --> 00:06:03,878
so you may not be able to see the files even after applying.

115
00:06:05,178 --> 00:06:07,608
- Okay. - The review takes 2 to 3 weeks.

116
00:06:09,418 --> 00:06:10,418
Father.

117
00:06:11,448 --> 00:06:12,888
Will I finally find out this time?

118
00:06:14,348 --> 00:06:17,158
What happened that day?

119
00:06:21,188 --> 00:06:22,188
I'm sorry.

120
00:06:23,398 --> 00:06:24,858
I'm sorry I can't remember anything.

121
00:06:35,438 --> 00:06:36,438
Yes, General Director Ko.

122
00:06:38,178 --> 00:06:40,308
What? President Ko?

123
00:06:46,048 --> 00:06:47,248
(View Now)

124
00:06:52,018 --> 00:06:53,188
(Seoul Citizen Daily)

125
00:06:53,258 --> 00:06:55,898
(May 16, 2001, 10:40pm Car Rear-End Collision, Jeongbin-Gu)

126
00:06:56,698 --> 00:06:57,858
I found it!

127
00:06:58,968 --> 00:07:01,167
What? What did you find?

128
00:07:01,168 --> 00:07:02,868
Oh, it's nothing.

129
00:07:03,338 --> 00:07:04,338
I'm sorry.

130
00:07:09,838 --> 00:07:12,037
Don't you think something's going on...

131
00:07:12,038 --> 00:07:13,208
with Team Leader Ko and Jo Eun Ae lately?

132
00:07:14,248 --> 00:07:15,448
Now that you mention it.

133
00:07:15,948 --> 00:07:17,478
Well, I'm not sure about Eun Ae,

134
00:07:17,548 --> 00:07:20,118
but Team Leader Ko has seemed pretty down lately.

135
00:07:20,288 --> 00:07:22,388
It's not like they can be happy all the time.

136
00:07:23,188 --> 00:07:24,258
What do you mean by that?

137
00:07:24,718 --> 00:07:27,158
What? Oh, it's nothing.

138
00:07:28,028 --> 00:07:29,658
Han Ji Hun, are you jealous?

139
00:07:30,258 --> 00:07:31,258
What?

140
00:07:31,958 --> 00:07:34,728
- Jealous? - Whenever they come up,

141
00:07:34,868 --> 00:07:36,298
you get a little cynical.

142
00:07:36,668 --> 00:07:38,568
It's almost like you hope things don't work out between them.

143
00:07:40,108 --> 00:07:41,468
When have I ever done that?

144
00:07:41,908 --> 00:07:43,508
Hey, don't go accusing an innocent person.

145
00:07:44,578 --> 00:07:47,008
Team Leader Ko, where are you? I think I found it.

146
00:07:47,408 --> 00:07:50,347
I searched all the major daily papers, and nothing came up

147
00:07:50,348 --> 00:07:53,088
so I fed the information to Joy, and it just popped up now.

148
00:07:54,018 --> 00:07:56,058
It's a short article from a local paper,

149
00:07:56,558 --> 00:07:57,918
so hurry back.

150
00:08:00,088 --> 00:08:01,228
- Jo Eun Ae. - Yes.

151
00:08:01,958 --> 00:08:03,158
Do you have a moment?

152
00:08:03,828 --> 00:08:05,028
Yes, of course.

153
00:08:05,098 --> 00:08:06,668
(Conference Room)

154
00:08:09,838 --> 00:08:12,968
After attending the living funeral, I started thinking.

155
00:08:13,668 --> 00:08:17,608
If I were to hold my own funeral, who would I invite?

156
00:08:18,778 --> 00:08:21,047
Who would I want to hold hands with one last time...

157
00:08:21,048 --> 00:08:23,678
and share one last meal with?

158
00:08:26,718 --> 00:08:27,718
My family.

159
00:08:28,888 --> 00:08:31,888
And after them, I thought of Team Leader Ko.

160
00:08:34,428 --> 00:08:36,328
Don't get me wrong.

161
00:08:36,698 --> 00:08:40,268
I'm just saying that Team Leader Ko is like family to me.

162
00:08:40,568 --> 00:08:41,998
I won't.

163
00:08:42,328 --> 00:08:44,268
I completely understand what you mean.

164
00:08:44,798 --> 00:08:46,838
I heard from General Director Ko that...

165
00:08:46,908 --> 00:08:49,678
Team Leader Ko is looking for old accident records?

166
00:08:49,738 --> 00:08:51,178
You heard about that?

167
00:08:51,878 --> 00:08:56,278
Team Leader Ko wants to recover his lost memories.

168
00:08:58,378 --> 00:09:00,888
I thought I heard you say you had found something.

169
00:09:01,148 --> 00:09:02,288
I did.

170
00:09:02,618 --> 00:09:05,688
The local police station didn't have any records of the accident,

171
00:09:05,758 --> 00:09:08,988
so Team Leader Ko went to the prosecutor's office to check.

172
00:09:09,128 --> 00:09:12,668
But I think I just found the article about the accident.

173
00:09:12,828 --> 00:09:13,828
You did?

174
00:09:14,498 --> 00:09:17,468
I can't imagine it was easy finding records for an accident that old.

175
00:09:17,738 --> 00:09:19,638
Yes, I finally found it,

176
00:09:20,068 --> 00:09:22,238
but I'm not sure how helpful it'll be.

177
00:09:23,178 --> 00:09:24,278
Team Leader Ko...

178
00:09:24,838 --> 00:09:27,478
His birthday is the same day as his father's death anniversary,

179
00:09:28,078 --> 00:09:29,948
so he's never celebrated it.

180
00:09:31,478 --> 00:09:33,618
He hasn't been able to open up to anyone,

181
00:09:33,988 --> 00:09:35,488
and he's lived a lonely life.

182
00:09:35,858 --> 00:09:37,658
It must have been because of that trauma.

183
00:09:38,018 --> 00:09:40,228
Yes, I had a feeling.

184
00:09:40,458 --> 00:09:43,228
You're the one who managed to open Team Leader Ko's heart...

185
00:09:43,298 --> 00:09:45,768
when no one else could, so I'm sure you'll do fine.

186
00:09:46,328 --> 00:09:47,598
But I really hope that this time,

187
00:09:48,528 --> 00:09:51,068
he can get his lost memories back...

188
00:09:51,838 --> 00:09:53,868
and overcome his pain.

189
00:09:54,268 --> 00:09:55,978
Yes, that's what we're hoping for.

190
00:09:57,278 --> 00:10:00,978
And if you need my help, please let me know.

191
00:10:01,348 --> 00:10:02,348
Yes, Ms. Seo.

192
00:10:06,048 --> 00:10:08,648
You didn't have to pack me a lunch today.

193
00:10:09,088 --> 00:10:12,018
Why? You said you didn't like eating out.

194
00:10:12,118 --> 00:10:15,828
We're on an alternating lunch schedule.

195
00:10:15,898 --> 00:10:17,828
An alter-what?

196
00:10:17,898 --> 00:10:21,128
Alternating. I take the even days.

197
00:10:22,068 --> 00:10:23,538
Anyway, today is Bung Woo's...

198
00:10:24,668 --> 00:10:26,438
No, it's the day Writer Seo packs lunch.

199
00:10:27,438 --> 00:10:29,408
So you two are using work as an excuse to hang out?

200
00:10:29,478 --> 00:10:33,048
Mom, I've been following my curfew perfectly these days,

201
00:10:33,108 --> 00:10:34,378
so no nagging.

202
00:10:35,748 --> 00:10:39,418
The webtoon we worked on together will be released in a week.

203
00:10:39,948 --> 00:10:42,018
How is it? Think it'll do well?

204
00:10:42,088 --> 00:10:44,388
Of course. Look who wrote it and who drew it.

205
00:10:44,588 --> 00:10:49,498
Is he any good? He seems a bit flaky.

206
00:10:49,628 --> 00:10:51,027
What are you talking about?

207
00:10:51,028 --> 00:10:55,298
Mom, no one understands my story better than Bung Woo.

208
00:10:55,798 --> 00:10:58,098
We're going to be a huge success.

209
00:10:58,398 --> 00:11:00,038
Okay, then. Make it a huge hit.

210
00:11:00,738 --> 00:11:03,738
And since I already packed this, take it and eat it.

211
00:11:04,008 --> 00:11:05,478
- Okay. - Okay.

212
00:11:06,608 --> 00:11:10,278
- I'm leaving. - Okay, don't forget your curfew.

213
00:11:18,358 --> 00:11:19,358
Yes, Mom.

214
00:11:20,688 --> 00:11:21,688
Lunch?

215
00:11:22,928 --> 00:11:24,798
No, I don't think I'll go today.

216
00:11:25,898 --> 00:11:27,168
I have a lot to do at home,

217
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:29,238
and I should be considerate of Min Ho's mom.

218
00:11:29,538 --> 00:11:30,798
Why Min Ho's mom?

219
00:11:31,868 --> 00:11:33,608
Why are you walking on eggshells around her?

220
00:11:34,008 --> 00:11:35,977
I'm not walking on eggshells.

221
00:11:35,978 --> 00:11:37,278
But from Min Ho's mom's perspective,

222
00:11:37,338 --> 00:11:40,378
an unexpected sister-in-law showing up must be stressful.

223
00:11:42,378 --> 00:11:45,888
Yes, let's have lunch at my place next time.

224
00:11:47,048 --> 00:11:48,048
Okay.

225
00:11:52,888 --> 00:11:56,558
Are the lunches packed? Let's see.

226
00:11:57,498 --> 00:11:58,498
Is that all?

227
00:11:58,558 --> 00:11:59,668
Who is this tiny portion supposed to feed?

228
00:11:59,928 --> 00:12:02,568
What do you mean, tiny? It's a perfect single serving.

229
00:12:02,998 --> 00:12:05,297
That's my point. Why is it only for one person?

230
00:12:05,298 --> 00:12:07,168
You could have packed more when you were making it.

231
00:12:07,408 --> 00:12:11,278
Do it again. Pack some more for me.

232
00:12:11,538 --> 00:12:14,078
You little brat. Did you think I wouldn't know?

233
00:12:14,508 --> 00:12:17,077
You're always asking for huge lunches.

234
00:12:17,078 --> 00:12:18,848
You've been giving them all to that girl, haven't you?

235
00:12:19,118 --> 00:12:20,888
Giving them to her? What are you talking about?

236
00:12:21,248 --> 00:12:23,758
Bung Nim always packs a big lunch for two anyway.

237
00:12:23,988 --> 00:12:26,328
I told you. She's not the one for you.

238
00:12:27,528 --> 00:12:29,328
A softie like you...

239
00:12:29,428 --> 00:12:31,398
should never be with a strong-willed girl like her.

240
00:12:31,528 --> 00:12:36,838
A woman should be sweet, kind, and gentle like me.

241
00:12:37,068 --> 00:12:38,338
No way.

242
00:12:38,468 --> 00:12:40,438
You, gentle?

243
00:12:41,238 --> 00:12:42,877
Whatever. Anyway, next time you pack my lunch...

244
00:12:42,878 --> 00:12:44,037
What are they called again?

245
00:12:44,038 --> 00:12:45,678
Right. Make me some bibi rolls.

246
00:12:45,738 --> 00:12:48,207
- What? Bibi rolls? - You know the ones.

247
00:12:48,208 --> 00:12:50,918
The ones with bibimbap on a wheat crepe that you roll up.

248
00:12:51,078 --> 00:12:52,348
They're so delicious.

249
00:12:52,748 --> 00:12:56,318
Get out of here before I decide to roll you up instead.

250
00:12:56,588 --> 00:12:59,628
And you call yourself gentle?

251
00:12:59,928 --> 00:13:03,028
Terrifying is more like it. Goodness.

252
00:13:03,628 --> 00:13:04,658
I'm heading out.

253
00:13:05,858 --> 00:13:06,868
I swear.

254
00:13:29,088 --> 00:13:30,718
(Confirm Chairman's Breakfast Schedule)

255
00:13:33,828 --> 00:13:35,558
(Jeongbin Police Station, Traffic Investigation Unit Number)

256
00:13:36,498 --> 00:13:37,498
What's this?

257
00:13:39,528 --> 00:13:41,898
"Request for a traffic accident report."

258
00:13:42,868 --> 00:13:43,868
"2001?"

259
00:13:46,808 --> 00:13:48,368
What traffic accident was that?

260
00:13:49,708 --> 00:13:51,038
After the business went bankrupt,

261
00:13:51,708 --> 00:13:54,148
he was at the Gangsu Construction overseas branch.

262
00:13:57,078 --> 00:14:00,488
Is this another one of the Chairman's background checks?

263
00:14:22,368 --> 00:14:23,378
Honestly.

264
00:14:24,538 --> 00:14:26,108
Eun Ae made this?

265
00:14:27,278 --> 00:14:29,308
She takes such good care of her boyfriend,

266
00:14:29,378 --> 00:14:30,748
even though she's all thumbs.

267
00:14:42,088 --> 00:14:44,557
Goodness. The son...

268
00:14:44,558 --> 00:14:46,828
and father are spitting images of each other.

269
00:14:47,298 --> 00:14:48,928
No wonder he looked familiar.

270
00:14:51,568 --> 00:14:54,708
Why did you have to leave so soon and make your son so lonely?

271
00:14:57,078 --> 00:14:59,948
Don't you worry. All of us...

272
00:15:00,848 --> 00:15:02,478
will make sure he's not lonely.

273
00:15:12,058 --> 00:15:13,058
That day,

274
00:15:13,628 --> 00:15:16,158
you couldn't really enjoy yourself because of me, could you?

275
00:15:16,798 --> 00:15:21,328
Not at all. Everyone was having a blast.

276
00:15:22,698 --> 00:15:24,268
I was very worried,

277
00:15:24,798 --> 00:15:26,938
but you're playing janggi with me again,

278
00:15:27,238 --> 00:15:29,438
and I'm so relieved, Chairman.

279
00:15:29,978 --> 00:15:33,878
You looked really close with that owner of the pancake restaurant.

280
00:15:34,348 --> 00:15:35,448
It's very nice to see.

281
00:15:36,048 --> 00:15:38,178
Pardon? You mean her?

282
00:15:39,888 --> 00:15:43,658
I wasn't sure at first, but we have great conversations.

283
00:15:44,358 --> 00:15:47,428
It feels like I've made a good friend in my old age.

284
00:15:48,058 --> 00:15:50,658
I'm glad you've made a good friend.

285
00:15:51,558 --> 00:15:53,628
The most important things when you get older...

286
00:15:54,128 --> 00:15:56,298
are your health and your friends.

287
00:15:56,868 --> 00:16:01,338
Yes. If only we'd had a little more time yesterday...

288
00:16:01,668 --> 00:16:04,508
We were going to perform a line dance for you.

289
00:16:04,808 --> 00:16:07,308
It's a shame we couldn't show you.

290
00:16:07,978 --> 00:16:11,418
Then I'll arrange a time, so you can show me.

291
00:16:11,548 --> 00:16:13,248
Really? Should we?

292
00:16:15,088 --> 00:16:16,588
Checkmate.

293
00:16:17,358 --> 00:16:20,188
Darn it, you caught me off guard.

294
00:16:21,028 --> 00:16:22,358
Are you finished?

295
00:16:23,258 --> 00:16:26,597
I made acorn jelly soup for lunch. Please come in.

296
00:16:26,598 --> 00:16:29,028
Acorn jelly soup? Sounds great.

297
00:16:29,538 --> 00:16:31,537
Thanks to Madam,

298
00:16:31,538 --> 00:16:34,268
looks like we're having genuine acorn jelly soup today.

299
00:16:34,968 --> 00:16:37,438
You go on ahead. I'll clean up and come in.

300
00:16:38,708 --> 00:16:39,747
Goodness.

301
00:16:39,748 --> 00:16:43,848
Hello. How are you, sir?

302
00:16:44,078 --> 00:16:46,287
- Very well. Thank you very much. - Hey...

303
00:16:46,288 --> 00:16:49,718
Madam made some acorn jelly soup.

304
00:16:50,018 --> 00:16:52,518
- Would you join us for a bowl? - What did you say?

305
00:16:52,588 --> 00:16:54,457
Join us for some acorn jelly soup.

306
00:16:54,458 --> 00:16:55,788
Acorn jelly soup.

307
00:16:57,858 --> 00:16:58,858
Listen,

308
00:16:59,128 --> 00:17:01,227
I've tolerated you until now...

309
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:03,097
since you've lived longer in this house,

310
00:17:03,098 --> 00:17:04,098
and you're the old-timer,

311
00:17:04,168 --> 00:17:08,068
- but I can't take it anymore. - What? Can't take what?

312
00:17:08,138 --> 00:17:09,878
What did you just say to me?

313
00:17:10,208 --> 00:17:11,738
That you're going to make me into acorn jelly soup?

314
00:17:12,408 --> 00:17:13,948
Just because my husband is easy-going...

315
00:17:14,008 --> 00:17:15,408
and calls you by a friendly title,

316
00:17:15,478 --> 00:17:16,918
you think you can get away with anything, don't you?

317
00:17:16,978 --> 00:17:20,448
Good grief. When did I say I'd make you into acorn jelly soup?

318
00:17:20,718 --> 00:17:24,588
I said the Madam made some and that you should have a bowl.

319
00:17:24,688 --> 00:17:25,688
What?

320
00:17:25,958 --> 00:17:29,898
- So I didn't hear you correctly? - Give me a break. Honestly.

321
00:17:29,958 --> 00:17:30,958
I'm not eating it.

322
00:17:30,959 --> 00:17:32,498
The name is so unpleasant, so I've lost my appetite.

323
00:17:32,598 --> 00:17:35,468
Seriously. What kind of a name is that?

324
00:17:35,798 --> 00:17:37,238
Fine, whatever.

325
00:17:38,598 --> 00:17:41,468
Gosh, one of these days, that man and I...

326
00:17:41,638 --> 00:17:43,738
are going to have a proper showdown.

327
00:17:46,578 --> 00:17:49,578
Oh, Father. Are you eating acorn jelly soup?

328
00:17:49,648 --> 00:17:52,118
Yes. You should come have a bowl, too.

329
00:17:52,318 --> 00:17:54,448
No, thank you. I'm fine.

330
00:17:56,318 --> 00:17:58,018
It's so savoury and rich.

331
00:17:58,558 --> 00:18:00,058
The broth is just perfect.

332
00:18:01,328 --> 00:18:04,058
It's the cold noodle broth Yeon Soon brought over last time.

333
00:18:04,298 --> 00:18:06,698
I froze it and used it for this.

334
00:18:06,928 --> 00:18:10,138
Yeon Soon's cooking is just like yours.

335
00:18:10,538 --> 00:18:15,368
Yes. Her looks, her kindness, her cooking skills...

336
00:18:15,538 --> 00:18:19,078
There's really not a single thing to dislike about her.

337
00:18:21,208 --> 00:18:22,208
I agree.

338
00:18:22,608 --> 00:18:25,148
She and her husband are both so upright and thoughtful.

339
00:18:25,518 --> 00:18:26,948
They're the real deal.

340
00:18:27,518 --> 00:18:31,058
Oh, my. Yeon Soon's ears must be burning right now.

341
00:18:32,158 --> 00:18:34,988
Aren't you a little upset about Yeon Soon?

342
00:18:35,288 --> 00:18:37,528
That you couldn't register her as your daughter.

343
00:18:38,028 --> 00:18:39,698
I wouldn't say upset.

344
00:18:40,468 --> 00:18:41,868
It's more of a great shame.

345
00:18:42,628 --> 00:18:45,068
But I know why she refused.

346
00:18:45,798 --> 00:18:46,868
What?

347
00:18:47,268 --> 00:18:49,037
She refused to be recognised...

348
00:18:49,038 --> 00:18:51,678
as the Chairman of Gangsu Group's daughter?

349
00:18:51,878 --> 00:18:53,048
That's right.

350
00:18:53,578 --> 00:18:56,078
She knows Gyeol and Eun Ae are in love with each other.

351
00:18:56,678 --> 00:19:00,218
And that putting her name on the registry would hurt them.

352
00:19:01,148 --> 00:19:02,288
Oh, my goodness.

353
00:19:02,648 --> 00:19:06,158
That couldn't have been an easy decision to make.

354
00:19:06,328 --> 00:19:08,288
Excuse me, mister,

355
00:19:08,688 --> 00:19:10,158
but what if she hadn't made that decision?

356
00:19:10,598 --> 00:19:13,128
If she were on the registry, they'd legally be first cousins.

357
00:19:13,528 --> 00:19:18,338
Well, regardless of the paperwork, they aren't related by blood.

358
00:19:18,438 --> 00:19:20,767
Why not try persuading her again?

359
00:19:20,768 --> 00:19:22,707
- Mister! - Goodness.

360
00:19:22,708 --> 00:19:25,678
Why don't you just eat your acorn jelly soup...

361
00:19:25,778 --> 00:19:27,708
and stay out of our family's business?

362
00:19:27,948 --> 00:19:29,248
That's enough.

363
00:19:29,748 --> 00:19:31,118
How dare you speak to an elder that way?

364
00:19:31,448 --> 00:19:32,448
Apologise.

365
00:19:32,678 --> 00:19:36,618
He should know when to stop. Meddling in our family's business.

366
00:19:36,688 --> 00:19:37,688
I said...

367
00:19:39,118 --> 00:19:40,288
I'm sorry, mister.

368
00:19:41,288 --> 00:19:43,798
Right. Since I'm the older one here,

369
00:19:44,328 --> 00:19:46,098
I suppose I have to be the bigger person.

370
00:19:46,628 --> 00:19:47,898
I'll be going now.

371
00:19:51,938 --> 00:19:56,638
Oh, dear. When will she ever let go of her greed?

372
00:19:56,708 --> 00:19:58,008
Unbelievable.

373
00:20:08,948 --> 00:20:10,758
Honey, listen.

374
00:20:11,058 --> 00:20:12,657
That Yong Man gets my blood pressure so high,

375
00:20:12,658 --> 00:20:14,428
I can barely stand it.

376
00:20:14,488 --> 00:20:15,558
(President Ko Dae Chi)

377
00:20:15,628 --> 00:20:17,628
What's wrong now?

378
00:20:17,928 --> 00:20:19,258
Who does that man think he is?

379
00:20:19,658 --> 00:20:23,798
He finds fault with everything I do. I can't stand it anymore.

380
00:20:23,898 --> 00:20:25,568
Fire Yong Man right now.

381
00:20:26,368 --> 00:20:27,368
Crystal.

382
00:20:27,568 --> 00:20:29,667
Your husband isn't exactly at leisure,

383
00:20:29,668 --> 00:20:32,008
and he's not in the mood for your complaining.

384
00:20:32,238 --> 00:20:33,808
- So let's hang up. - Honey,

385
00:20:33,948 --> 00:20:37,648
this isn't me whining. Right now, in front of Father,

386
00:20:37,878 --> 00:20:41,017
Yong Man says it won't be a problem for Gyeol and Eun Ae...

387
00:20:41,018 --> 00:20:42,488
if Kang Yeon Ja is put on the family register,

388
00:20:42,548 --> 00:20:44,458
and he said to convince Kang Yeon Ja again.

389
00:20:44,518 --> 00:20:46,158
That's what's happening.

390
00:20:46,688 --> 00:20:49,188
What? That guy, seriously.

391
00:20:51,398 --> 00:20:54,027
All right. I'll leave work early and talk to Yong Man.

392
00:20:54,028 --> 00:20:55,228
Now hang up.

393
00:20:55,728 --> 00:20:57,498
Honey!

394
00:20:58,398 --> 00:20:59,498
Darn it. Unbelievable.

395
00:21:01,908 --> 00:21:02,908
Yes.

396
00:21:03,438 --> 00:21:04,478
You wanted to see me?

397
00:21:05,208 --> 00:21:06,208
Sit down.

398
00:21:06,948 --> 00:21:07,948
Yes.

399
00:21:08,008 --> 00:21:10,748
(Gangsu Construction)

400
00:21:13,988 --> 00:21:16,758
What's with your work ethic lately?

401
00:21:17,158 --> 00:21:18,158
Excuse me?

402
00:21:18,558 --> 00:21:20,088
Since last week, you've been constantly...

403
00:21:20,158 --> 00:21:21,558
taking half-days and coming in late.

404
00:21:22,088 --> 00:21:23,128
What's that all about?

405
00:21:23,328 --> 00:21:27,698
I am merely using the vacation days, which I am legally entitled to.

406
00:21:27,968 --> 00:21:29,428
What? Legally entitled?

407
00:21:30,538 --> 00:21:32,937
Do you think you can just take all your vacation days...

408
00:21:32,938 --> 00:21:34,538
whenever you want?

409
00:21:37,178 --> 00:21:39,738
Of course, for a regular employee,

410
00:21:40,208 --> 00:21:42,308
there's nothing wrong with using their vacation time.

411
00:21:42,978 --> 00:21:44,278
But you are different.

412
00:21:46,848 --> 00:21:48,648
You're not just any employee.

413
00:21:49,048 --> 00:21:52,187
You're Gangsu Group's future chairman and my son.

414
00:21:52,188 --> 00:21:53,288
Father,

415
00:21:53,688 --> 00:21:56,188
if you would please point out exactly what I did wrong...

416
00:21:57,558 --> 00:21:58,558
You.

417
00:21:59,398 --> 00:22:01,228
How much time is left until the third competition?

418
00:22:01,968 --> 00:22:03,638
Just two months.

419
00:22:04,068 --> 00:22:06,237
Do you really think you can prepare for it properly?

420
00:22:06,238 --> 00:22:09,038
Yes, I am doing my best to prepare for the competition.

421
00:22:09,338 --> 00:22:11,908
That's what you think. Is this company a joke to you?

422
00:22:12,578 --> 00:22:14,777
The Retirement Community project that Grandfather gave you...

423
00:22:14,778 --> 00:22:16,148
as a mission for the succession...

424
00:22:16,618 --> 00:22:18,378
is a project that will secure this company's next 100 years.

425
00:22:18,678 --> 00:22:21,618
- Do you get it? - Yes, I'm fully aware of that.

426
00:22:21,948 --> 00:22:23,388
Then why does someone who's aware of that...

427
00:22:23,458 --> 00:22:25,188
keep taking half-days off for personal business?

428
00:22:29,428 --> 00:22:30,458
Your team.

429
00:22:31,228 --> 00:22:32,658
Have you finished selecting the candidate sites?

430
00:22:33,098 --> 00:22:35,098
Yes, we're considering it from all angles.

431
00:22:35,198 --> 00:22:37,898
Considering? While taking off two or three times a week?

432
00:22:37,968 --> 00:22:38,998
You call that considering?

433
00:22:40,438 --> 00:22:43,507
From now on, no more personal leave.

434
00:22:43,508 --> 00:22:44,638
This is...

435
00:22:45,208 --> 00:22:47,248
an order from me as your father and the president.

436
00:22:48,178 --> 00:22:49,248
Understand?

437
00:22:50,518 --> 00:22:51,518
Understood.

438
00:22:51,878 --> 00:22:53,687
I will do my best not to take time off...

439
00:22:53,688 --> 00:22:54,918
during work hours from now on.

440
00:22:56,888 --> 00:22:57,888
And...

441
00:22:59,318 --> 00:23:02,288
I will approve of your relationship with the intern, Jo Eun Ae.

442
00:23:03,858 --> 00:23:04,858
Excuse me?

443
00:23:05,558 --> 00:23:08,468
It's not that I was against you two from the start.

444
00:23:08,868 --> 00:23:11,798
But lately, we were discussing adding...

445
00:23:12,598 --> 00:23:15,138
Jo Eun Ae's mother to our family register.

446
00:23:16,138 --> 00:23:18,507
If that happened, you two would become cousins on paper.

447
00:23:18,508 --> 00:23:20,348
That's why I was against it.

448
00:23:21,378 --> 00:23:23,578
But Kang Yeon Ja has decided to give up on it.

449
00:23:24,748 --> 00:23:26,478
She won't be added to our family register.

450
00:23:27,288 --> 00:23:28,288
What?

451
00:23:28,388 --> 00:23:31,318
I suppose it means she doesn't want to be an obstacle for you two.

452
00:23:32,658 --> 00:23:35,458
For a mother and daughter who just met after 50 years,

453
00:23:36,528 --> 00:23:37,958
it couldn't have been an easy decision.

454
00:23:39,498 --> 00:23:40,498
Yes.

455
00:23:42,928 --> 00:23:45,668
By the way, where were you today?

456
00:23:46,468 --> 00:23:48,408
I just came from the prosecutor's office.

457
00:23:49,468 --> 00:23:50,478
The pro...

458
00:23:50,978 --> 00:23:52,008
The prosecutor's office?

459
00:23:52,508 --> 00:23:53,848
What were you doing there?

460
00:23:54,148 --> 00:23:56,508
I'm sorry, but it's not work-related.

461
00:23:56,918 --> 00:23:58,318
Please excuse me.

462
00:23:58,978 --> 00:24:02,048
(Gangsu Construction)

463
00:24:04,358 --> 00:24:05,358
Seriously.

464
00:24:05,918 --> 00:24:08,558
What is that kid thinking?

465
00:24:09,588 --> 00:24:13,328
He lived quietly for 25 years. He should've just kept it that way.

466
00:24:17,398 --> 00:24:19,498
(Strategic Planning Division)

467
00:24:20,238 --> 00:24:21,708
Looks like everyone from Team One has gone home.

468
00:24:22,138 --> 00:24:24,578
I'm sorry. The meeting ran late because of me.

469
00:24:24,638 --> 00:24:25,838
Oh, not at all.

470
00:24:26,108 --> 00:24:28,808
You were on leave, yet you came back in the afternoon for a meeting.

471
00:24:29,648 --> 00:24:31,277
Thank you, Kim Sung Guk.

472
00:24:31,278 --> 00:24:33,148
I appreciate your always-perfect data support.

473
00:24:33,318 --> 00:24:35,518
Not at all. I was just doing my job.

474
00:24:36,048 --> 00:24:37,458
Well, I'll be heading home now.

475
00:24:38,788 --> 00:24:41,228
- Goodbye, Mr. Kim. - Good night.

476
00:24:42,128 --> 00:24:43,798
So, how did your errand go?

477
00:24:44,228 --> 00:24:46,298
I couldn't ask because of the meeting we had right away.

478
00:24:47,328 --> 00:24:49,198
Luckily, the prosecutor's office still had the files,

479
00:24:49,268 --> 00:24:50,598
so I submitted a request to view them.

480
00:24:51,298 --> 00:24:53,467
But that doesn't mean I'll be able to see everything.

481
00:24:53,468 --> 00:24:55,708
They said depending on their review, I might not get access.

482
00:24:56,168 --> 00:24:58,208
And it'll take two or three weeks to get the results.

483
00:24:58,378 --> 00:25:00,208
What? That long?

484
00:25:00,948 --> 00:25:02,908
Oh, and what was that article you said you found earlier?

485
00:25:03,078 --> 00:25:04,548
Oh, yes. The article about the car accident...

486
00:25:04,618 --> 00:25:05,618
on May 16, 2001.

487
00:25:05,678 --> 00:25:07,018
I couldn't find it no matter how hard I looked,

488
00:25:07,148 --> 00:25:09,088
but this is a news brief I found using Joy.

489
00:25:14,058 --> 00:25:18,128
Have you figured out the exact flow of funds yet?

490
00:25:18,528 --> 00:25:21,128
Yes, it's going to take some more time.

491
00:25:21,328 --> 00:25:24,168
The account in Switzerland isn't easily accessible.

492
00:25:25,268 --> 00:25:26,298
But why...

493
00:25:28,138 --> 00:25:29,338
Are you all right, Chairman?

494
00:25:30,138 --> 00:25:31,838
I have to be. What choice do I have?

495
00:25:33,278 --> 00:25:34,948
It's not like I just found out.

496
00:25:35,648 --> 00:25:37,278
I don't know what I'm going to do...

497
00:25:38,578 --> 00:25:41,388
If it were up to me, I'd deal with President Ko right now.

498
00:25:42,448 --> 00:25:45,558
Chairman, now is not the time to expose this.

499
00:25:46,688 --> 00:25:47,988
What are you talking about?

500
00:25:48,728 --> 00:25:51,128
I don't have time to finish this.

501
00:25:51,398 --> 00:25:53,158
That's all the more reason you must wait.

502
00:25:54,328 --> 00:25:56,428
With what we know about the money trail now,

503
00:25:56,498 --> 00:25:58,138
it's not enough to fix everything.

504
00:25:58,898 --> 00:26:02,808
I will find something big soon and report back to you.

505
00:26:05,578 --> 00:26:06,608
Did...

506
00:26:07,248 --> 00:26:10,247
something happen at my funeral?

507
00:26:10,248 --> 00:26:11,448
Pardon?

508
00:26:11,978 --> 00:26:15,088
Oh, no. Nothing happened.

509
00:26:15,718 --> 00:26:19,088
Then why did you just leave? That's not like you, Chief Seo.

510
00:26:19,718 --> 00:26:20,758
I'm sorry, Chairman.

511
00:26:21,558 --> 00:26:23,998
I wasn't feeling well that day.

512
00:26:36,338 --> 00:26:37,638
Yes, Chief Financial Officer.

513
00:26:39,808 --> 00:26:42,948
What? Seo Gwon Sik is investigating me?

514
00:26:44,478 --> 00:26:46,348
- What? - For the time being,

515
00:26:46,788 --> 00:26:48,188
lay low for a while.

516
00:26:48,588 --> 00:26:49,588
I'm hanging up.

517
00:27:00,698 --> 00:27:01,698
Seo Gwon Sik.

518
00:27:02,868 --> 00:27:03,868
What is your problem?

519
00:27:06,598 --> 00:27:08,768
What are you, some kind of mole?

520
00:27:09,738 --> 00:27:11,907
Now that you're done with the mother-daughter search,

521
00:27:11,908 --> 00:27:13,308
you're investigating me?

522
00:27:14,608 --> 00:27:16,148
What makes you so high and mighty?

523
00:27:18,278 --> 00:27:19,378
You're a murderer.

524
00:27:21,588 --> 00:27:22,588
What?

525
00:27:23,188 --> 00:27:24,288
Am I wrong?

526
00:27:25,458 --> 00:27:26,558
I'm right, aren't I?

527
00:27:26,928 --> 00:27:28,628
You're the murderer who killed Han Su Cheol.

528
00:27:51,518 --> 00:27:54,217
(Our Happy Days)

529
00:27:54,218 --> 00:27:56,648
I never should have gone to you 25 years ago.

530
00:27:56,858 --> 00:27:58,858
If only I hadn't gone to see you then.

531
00:27:58,918 --> 00:28:01,728
If you two hadn't shown up 25 years ago...

532
00:28:01,788 --> 00:28:03,798
I saw a strange memo.

533
00:28:03,858 --> 00:28:06,968
It mentioned a car accident in 2001 or something.

534
00:28:07,028 --> 00:28:08,828
If it's 2001? Could it be...

535
00:28:08,898 --> 00:28:10,238
Nothing happened between us.

536
00:28:10,568 --> 00:28:13,097
We just fell asleep at the desk, that's all.

537
00:28:13,098 --> 00:28:15,638
- What did you say? Get over here. - Stop!

538
00:28:15,768 --> 00:28:17,378
I like Bung Woo.

539
00:28:17,638 --> 00:28:18,778
Bung Nim.
